                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>Vice President Richard Nixon was in Libya
                    on December 12 and 13, 1953, as part of his goodwill trip to the Near and Far
                    East. While in Libya, he spoke with both King Idris and Prime Minister Muntasser. On his return, he spent the afternoons of December
                    21–23 at the Department <pb facs="0624" n="578" xml:id="pg578"/> of State,
                    discussing various aspects of his trip with Department officers. On January 8,
                    1954, he made a lengthy report to officers of the Department. Documentation on
                    this topic is in Department of State file 033.1100 NI/1–1854.</p>
            </div>
